; Probe 2 of the caret arc: `(: ^b str)` inside a product collects into one
; `(: return b)` member edge (AGENTS.md:107).
;
; Reads rc=0 once `valid_atom` carries the `^` arm.
; Compiles rc=0 TODAY AND IS WRONG: with no macro consuming the caret, the
; column is minted under the name `^result`. The macro cannot be written:
; recognising the `^` prefix off `(syntax_atom ?Node ?Text)` needs a text
; primitive, and the kernel op table at src/_6_eval/_4_kernel.rs:71-85 has
; none. `str.cons` is a decision (AGENTS.md:84), not a built op.
;
; Target shape, which compiles rc=0 on its own:
;   (: Pick (* (: source type) (: names any) (: result type) (: return result)))

(: Pick (* (: source type) (: names any) (: ^result type)))
